102:## Part 5 — Source-file handling
103-
104-See [[docs/ingest-workflows]] for source-file handling: filesystem-handle vs cite-key, source-page creation, deduplication, pre-populated frontmatter, and existing-pages-aware ingest discipline (including the Phase 1 rule that empty `products: []` on a food/personal-care paper is a defect).
105-
106:## Part 5b — Routing layer (system rule, not a per-session task)
107-
108-The wiki has a routing layer that is the system's responsibility, not the model's. No session, ingest or otherwise, is expected to maintain routing by hand. No prompt should ask the model to write routing rows directly. If a session finds itself maintaining routing by hand, that is a session-architecture failure to surface to Karen, not work to complete.
109-
110-### What routing is
111-
112-Routing is the mapping from each source to every product-category, ingredient, metal, and regulation page it should appear on. A single paper that measures "lead in 230 infant formulas, 192 cow-milk-based powders and 38 soy-based powders" should appear on the non-soy powder, soy-based powder, non-soy RTF, and soy-based RTF product pages (as direct evidence on the first two and broad-format-context on the second two), on `metals/lead`, and on the relevant cow-milk-derived and soy-protein-derived ingredient pages. The routing layer expresses that fan-out.
113-
114-The routing layer is the answer to a recurring failure mode: papers get ingested with frontmatter that correctly names the products and ingredients they touch, but no downstream process reads that frontmatter and fans the source out to the sibling pages. Without the routing layer, every later session has to re-derive routing from scratch, which is slow and lossy.
115-
116-### Where routing lives
117-
118-`data/evidence/product_source_routing_audit.csv` is the canonical routing artifact. One row per (source, target-page, route_kind) triple. The `route_kind` vocabulary is fixed: `direct_evidence`, `broad_formula_context`, `broad_powder_context`, `broad_product_context`, `exposure_only`, `regulatory_context`. Two sibling logs catch failures: `data/evidence/routing_unresolved.csv` (source frontmatter does not connect to any known target page) and `data/evidence/routing_malformed.csv` (source frontmatter is missing required fields).
119-
120-### How routing is maintained
121-
122-`tools/evidence/build-routing-audit.mjs` (or successor) reads every file in `wiki/sources/` and emits the audit. It runs on three triggers and is not invoked manually:
123-
124-1. File watcher: a `chokidar` watcher on `wiki/sources/` triggers a rebuild within seconds of any source page being created or modified. Runs as part of `npm run serve`.
125-2. Pre-commit hook: any commit touching `wiki/sources/` runs the audit and aborts if it cannot be regenerated cleanly.
126-3. Prebuild: `npm run build` runs the audit as part of the existing `prebuild` script. Build fails if the audit is stale or `routing_malformed.csv` is non-empty.
127-
128-### What models are responsible for during ingest
129-
130-The model writes the source page. It fills in frontmatter accurately, especially the `products`, `ingredients`, `matrices`, `metals`, and `jurisdictions` arrays, because those arrays are the routing layer's input. If a source touches infant formula generally without specifying soy vs non-soy, the frontmatter should say `matrices: [infant-formula]`, not `matrices: [infant-formula-powder-non-soy]`. The routing layer fans broad scopes out to sibling pages; the model does not pre-decide that fan-out by overspecifying frontmatter.
131-
132-### What models are NOT responsible for during ingest
133-
134-The model does not edit `product_source_routing_audit.csv`. The model does not update product-category page tables (those are regenerated by the generators in `tools/evidence/` downstream of the audit). The model does not maintain a mental map of which pages a source should land on. If a session attempts to maintain routing by hand or recompute fan-out per paper, that is a system failure to surface to Karen.
135-
136-The routing layer's output feeds the synthesis workflow in Part 9. When the audit reports that an (ingredient, metal) cell has accumulated a new contributing source, the synthesis pass reads the contributing sources together and updates the ingredient page's `contamination_profile`. The model writes source pages during ingest and runs synthesis as a separate workflow; the routing audit is what connects the two.
137-
138-### What lint catches
139-
140-The lint pass in Part 18 fails the build if `routing_unresolved.csv` is non-empty, `routing_malformed.csv` is non-empty, the routing audit's last-modified timestamp is older than any file in `wiki/sources/` (stale audit), or any product-category page references a source whose routing row has been removed (orphaned reference).
141-
142-For migration notes on pre-routing-layer pages, see [[docs/schema-history]].
143-
144:## Part 6 — Page templates
145-
146-See [[docs/page-templates]] for the full YAML schemas, section specifications, and mandatory-section lists for source / metal / ingredient / product-category / regulation / testing / microbiome / certification / course / app pages. Also covers audience layering, geographic and seasonal variance sub-fields, the three-field state system (`status`, `confidence`, `n_studies`), the coverage rule, and the body-table format.
147-
148-## Part 7 — Audience layering
149-
150-See [[docs/page-templates]] (Audience layering section). Every substantive page carries `audience: [regulator, educator, consumer, app]` in frontmatter; section-level `<!-- audience: ... -->` tagging allows one wiki to render three ways. Consumer translation must specify dose, population, and consumption frequency; never use undefined qualifiers ("small," "trace," "safe," "dangerous") without a quantitative anchor.
151-
152-## Part 8 — Ingest workflows
153-
154-See [[docs/ingest-workflows]] for the three workflows (single-paper, bulk, query), the Phase 0 prerequisite for new HMTc categories, the compiled-wiki rule (model/system/generator/Karen actor split), and the kickoff procedure.
155-
156-## Part 9 — Synthesis and re-synthesis
157-
158-Synthesis is the workflow that turns accumulated source-page evidence into the `contamination_profile` values on ingredient pages, the narrative summaries on metal pages, and the cross-source claims in regulation pages. **It is a workflow, not an ingest step.** Source pages get written during ingest; synthesis happens later, as a dedicated pass triggered either by the routing audit signaling that an ingredient/metal cell has new evidence or by Karen requesting it.
159-
160-This separation matters because synthesis is analytical work that requires reading multiple sources together. Doing it during ingest forces every ingest session to re-derive synthesis from scratch for every paper, which does not scale to 23,000 papers and produces drift across sessions. Doing it as a separate workflow, triggered when the evidence base for a cell crosses a threshold, lets each synthesis pass do the full job once and persist its result.
161-
162-### Trigger conditions
163-
164-A synthesis pass for a given (ingredient, metal) cell runs when any of:
165-
166-- The routing audit reports that the cell has accumulated a second contributing source since `last_reviewed`. Initial-population trigger: the cell moves from `status: pending` to `status: populated` with `confidence: low` and the first two-source synthesis.
167-- The cell's `n_studies` has doubled since `last_full_resynthesis` (resynthesize at 4, 8, 16, 32...). Periodic full-resynthesis trigger.
168-- A new source's values disagree with the current page state by more than 2x in either direction for `typical_ppb` or `p95_ppb`. Contradiction trigger.
169-- Two A-tier sources contradict each other on a synthesis claim. The pass arbitrates by re-reading both in full.
170-- Karen explicitly requests resynthesis.
171-
172-Triggers fire on the routing audit's signal, not on the ingest session's awareness. A bulk-ingest session does not run synthesis. A query session may trigger synthesis if Karen asks "what does the literature say about X" and the current synthesis is stale.
173-
174-### Synthesis modes
175-
176-- **Initial population** (first two sources): read both source pages in full; compute `typical_ppb`, `p95_ppb`, `n_studies: 2`, `confidence: low`; update the cell to `status: populated`; log the event to `data/evidence/review_events.jsonl`.
177-- **Incremental update** (after initial population): read the incoming paper plus the top 5 most-cited prior contributors; update values if warranted, increment `n_studies`, update `last_reviewed`, leave `last_full_resynthesis` unchanged. This is the middle path between naive overwriting (drifts) and full re-read (token-prohibitive at scale).
178-- **Full resynthesis** (n_studies doubled or trigger fired): identify every contributing source via wiki backlinks plus the routing audit; read each in full; recompute from the complete evidence set, not by patching existing values; update `last_full_resynthesis` and log the event with the trigger and value change.
179-
180-Every `contamination_profile` metal sub-block carries `last_reviewed`. The authoritative resynthesis history lives in `data/evidence/review_events.jsonl`; until that file is consistently populated, page-level fields are the working source of truth.
181-
182-### Downstream propagation rule
183-
184-When a synthesis page identifies implications for downstream wiki pages, the session that writes the synthesis page must also make those downstream edits in the same commit. Listing implications without executing them is a failure mode: it produces a to-do list that no future session will reliably pick up. The synthesis page records which downstream pages were updated and when, not what downstream pages need updating. If a downstream edit cannot be completed (target page does not exist, requires Karen's judgment, evidence too uncertain), log the specific blocker rather than writing a generic implication statement.
185-
186:## Part 10 — Page creation and naming
187-
188-New-page proposals (ingredient, product, regulation) surface from two places: the routing audit's `routing_unresolved.csv` when a source's frontmatter declares a page that does not exist, and the model's own pattern-noticing when a sub-variant accumulates enough independent evidence to warrant its own page. Either way, Karen approves before pages are created; the model does not silently invent ingredient or product pages mid-ingest.
189-
190-**Ingredients:** create a new page when 5 or more papers treat the sub-variant as a distinct commodity with its own risk profile. Below that threshold, add the variant as an `aliases` entry on the parent page with a short note in the page body. Example: 3 papers mention "rice bran" alongside rice papers → rice bran goes in `ingredients/rice.md` aliases. 10 papers focus specifically on rice bran contamination distinct from whole rice → create `ingredients/rice-bran.md`. When the threshold is crossed, propose the new page in the batch report.
191-
192-**Products:** product pages are auto-created as routing destinations whenever a source declares a slug with no matching page. Two entry points produce these:
193-
194-- `tools/autonomy/create-missing-pages.mjs` (frequency-driven, batch) handles slugs that have accumulated freq >= 2 across the corpus.
195-- `tools/autonomy/create-provisional-product-scaffold.mjs` (single-slug, on-demand) handles slugs the active ingest session encounters mid-run, including freq-1.
196-
197-Both tools mark the page `provisional_scaffold: true` plus `hmtc_category: pending_taxonomy_review` and `hmtc_row: pending_taxonomy_review` in frontmatter, and log creation to `data/evidence/provisional-product-scaffolds.jsonl`. **The flag is the governance signal:** the page exists so sources route somewhere defined, but HMTc category assignment, within-row clean/dirty splits, contamination-platform classification, and certification thresholds do not derive from the page until a Step 0 Lock is authored (see `tools/autonomy/cat<N>-step0-scaffold.mjs`; the Cat 2 scaffold is the reference exemplar). Scaffolding promotes the stub to a locked row, clearing the `provisional_scaffold` flag.
198-
199-The pre-2026-05-17 flag name `pending_category_lock: true` is the predecessor of `provisional_scaffold: true`. Both are recognized by audit-routing-discipline and the orchestrator for back-compat; new pages use `provisional_scaffold`. The pre-2026-05-17 policy of writing unresolved product slugs to `data/evidence/autonomy/product-stub-proposals-pending.csv` instead of creating pages is preserved as the `--no-products` flag for one-off cases. The default is to create the routing destination immediately.
200-
201-The 2026-05-14 incident (face-paint, lipstick, skin-lightening-cream auto-stubs retired the next day by the Cat 2 scaffold) was caused by stubs being created *without* a provisional flag — they looked like full product pages with HMTc bindings. The flag prevents that failure mode.
202-
203-**Ingredients (2026-05-17 update):** ingredient pages get the same treatment. Slugs at freq >= 2 are auto-stubbed by `create-missing-pages.mjs`; freq-1 slugs an active ingest declares are created via `tools/autonomy/create-provisional-ingredient-scaffold.mjs` with `provisional_scaffold: true` and `literature_scope: thin`. The 5-paper-threshold rule still applies to *promotion*: a provisional scaffold is the routing destination; it becomes a full ingredient page (with populated `contamination_profile`) once the literature crosses the threshold and the synthesis pass runs.
204-
205-**Regulations:** create a new regulation page on first encounter. Regulations have hard identifiers (rule numbers, official names) and benefit from being captured immediately.
206-
207-**Metals:** create a new metal page on first encounter, but only for metals that appear in the corpus with reasonable frequency. Exotic or trace metals stay as notes on related metal pages until they accumulate their own evidence base.
208-
209-**Merging.** Pages should occasionally be merged. If `ingredients/carrots.md` and `ingredients/root-vegetables.md` end up covering substantially the same literature with different framings, propose a merge in the next batch report. Claude does not merge pages autonomously.
210-
211-**Orphan prevention.** New pages must be linked from `index.md` on creation. They must also be linked from at least one parent category page (metal, ingredient, product, regulation, testing method) or they become orphans.
